he 2.5 million people have been  displaced here and there and almost a  half a million people are being hosted  in four countries Iraq Jordan Lebanon  and Turkey this humanitarian situation  as winter is approaching will be much  much more serious and we have to protect  the human rights and human dignity of  many people there and fourthly we have  to unite the international community's  very solid and form a will to resolve  this issue the international community  has been divided let alone the people  over Syrian themselves we cannot  continue like this way I have been  telling prisoners that listen to their  people most attentively and carefully  and to stop violence  unfortunately the recent proposal by the  Joint Special Representative Lakhdar  Brahimi and myself for a even briefer  polls during Muslim holiday has been  neglected ignored so many people have  been killed  now that the opposition forces seem to  be united with electing their own  coalition leader and since you hope that  the opposition also will move in a  coherent way so that dialogue can be  started  what is most important at this time all  the countries who have influence on  Syria must not provide the arms and  equipment and funds to a POTUS eyes this  will put their people only into a  greater misery this is not the way there  is no military solution  there should be a dialogue there should  be a political resolution in this United  Nations is a firmly committed and I'm  also very much committed in addressing  decision ultimately that what do you  think it will take to resolve the  conflict  artemiy tree there should be an end to  violence then the representatives of  both parties I should meet and try to  resolve this issue through dialogue and  a political resolution they should agree  on their future of their own this is the  Syrian people a syrian-led solution  that's the best way ok let's move on to  two of the big global challenges that  the UN is addressing climate change and  food security I think most people would  agree at this point that under  undeniably that there is global warming  taking place the bottom line is what is  the UN doing to help save the planet I'm  glad that you raised the issue of a  climate change since I became secretary  I have put this climate change issue at  the top of the global agenda I have been  trying to sound alarms to world  community that that we cannot continue  like this way we cannot burn our way to  prosperity without realizing the limit  of planet Earth if by human beings use  our planet  planet the limited resources like as we  are doing we may have to have another  planet unfortunately and reality in  reality is that we have only one planet  Earth not two and we don't have any a  plan B because we don't have any further  resources we are stepping over planetary  limitations that is why I have been  urging world leaders to first of all  agree on the legally binding treaty by  2015 this is an agreement by the world  leaders that we will have to agree on a  legally binding treaty by 2015 this is  an institution a legal institution but  we have to mobilize and necessary  funding we have to help many poor and  vulnerable group of people because they  do not have any capacity to adapt and  mitigate the impact of this a climate  change then we have to establish Green  Climate Fund about the three weeks ago  the world community has decided to  locate the headquarter of Green Climate  Fund in the Republic of Korea where they  will have to mobilize a hundred billion  dollars annually by 2020 then thereafter  every year 100 billion dollars to help  poor and developing countries this is  absolutely necessary through transfer of  technology by providing a financial  support we have to put the highest  political priority I was very glad when  President Obama in his recent election  night when he was a declared winner for  second term he said about this warming  planet  that means he has varied in his mind a  high priority on climate change I'm  ready to work with all the leaders apart  I believe that the United States should  lead this campaign United State is after  all the the world the richest and most  powerful country and they should lead by  example have you spoken with President  Obama about leading the cause I have  discussed this matter many times he has  been quite committed in 2009 when there  was the United Nations Climate Change  Conference in Copenhagen he himself  participated with world leaders all  through the night and I was very much  impressed since then we've been working  very hard to address all global  challenges climate change issues  sustainable development the global  health issues women empowerment energy  issues and global education issues all  these issues global challenges should be  addressed by global participation  through a collective political will do  you think that the majority of the  world's leaders are doing enough to  combat climate change are they adding  here I'm sorry to say that the world  leaders have not done enough they know  that there's a climate change causes  without without we got to any boundaries  national boundaries whether you are  coming from which or poor countries  whether you are coming from Asia Africa  Europe  it doesn't respect the national borders  as we have seen recently hurricane sandy  even though we cannot say that any we  cannot attribute any one course to to  the effect of Jesus Hurricane sandy but  we have seen these days extraordinarily  powerful and disastrous extreme weather  patterns it's getting worse and worse  and worse and worse this is definitely  caused by climate change phenomenon the  science has made it plainly clear that  and there's a human being which has been  causing this a climate change of  phenomena and therefore it should be  human being that to address this issue  by preventing from happening again we  have a moral and political  responsibility to handle avoid this a  planet earth 