l every woman every  child our ambition is that during  forthcoming five years we will save 16  million lives mostly women and girls and  the children this has gotten a lot of a  support from international  immunity how will you save them now by  providing food by providing nutrition's  and the by providing the necessary  sanitation and health to support this is  to provide to every women and every  child the healthy service because so  many women and girls are dying  needlessly from preventable diseases yes  what countries are you focusing on there  are many countries particularly poor  developing countries mostly in Africa  enable Latin America and also Southeast  Asian countries there are many many  women who are dying while giving do both  then why should a woman die to give a  both right the our target is that a  woman in South Sudan should live as a  woman in Sweden can live almost 100% of  women in European countries they live a  while giving birth but one out of five  women and dies while giving birth this  is injustice  so in acceptable situation great United  Nations is paying a great attention on  this I have raised this campaign at  partnership with Secretary Clinton of  the United States and it has cottoned I  think most support from intentional  community good good very good well I  would love to chat with you for the rest  of the afternoon but unfortunately I  know you have a lecture to give so I  thank you very much for being here with  us today  thank you very much it has been a great  pleasure let's work together to make  this world better for why would we need  the support from academic communities  anybody is like Yale yes problems of  this magnitude need everyone to work  together  thank you thinking  for more information about  secretary-general ban ki-moon please  visit to the United Nations website at  UN org /sg  be sure to join us again for another  episode of the Macmillan report made  possible through funding from the  Whitney and Betty M